  "generated_text": " find determine the residue of $-811\\pmod{24}$, we can use the properties of modular arithmetic.\n\nFirst, we divide $-811$ by $24$ to find the remainder. We can do this by finding the multiple of $24$ that is closest to $-811$.\n\nWe know that $24 \\times 34 = 816$, so we can write $-811$ as $-816 - 5$. This means that $-811$ is $5$ less than a multiple of $24$.\n\n,, we can find the residue of $-811\\pmod{24}$ by finding the remainder when $-5$ is divided by $24$. Since $-5$ is less than $24$, the remainder is simply $-5$.\n\nTherefore, the residue of $-811\\pmod{24}$ is $\\boxed{19}$.The answer is: 19",
